/-!
# VIII04 — existence, uniqueness and far-field matching (main root `viii04_main`)

Explicit pair (proved, not assumed): `b_*(R) = Qj/(n1 R)`, `v_*(R) = j/R² + n0 j/(n1 R³)`.
`viii04_main` (general non-extremal parameters `R_h > R_i ≥ 0`, `Q² = 3R_hR_i/4`, any real `j`):

0. the RN background is positive on `I = (R_h, ∞)` and satisfies all seven frozen PaperBVP relations
   with constants `(Q, 0)` on `I`;
1. existence: `(b_*, v_*) ∈ MagClass × VClass` and solves the ε-linearised frozen system on `I`;
2. uniqueness: any `(b, v) ∈ MagClass × VClass` solving it equals `(b_*, v_*)` on `I`;
3. matching: `R b(R) → Qj/n1` — the first-order magnetic far-field coefficient `a1^(1) = Qj/n1`
   is fixed by the two endpoint conditions together (the AF class alone only gives `b = O(1/R)`).
   That the AF class alone is *not* enough is formalised only for `Q = 0` (`horizon_necessity`, where the
   selected value is `0`); the `Q ≠ 0` analogue is not formalised.

Values of `b_*, v_*` outside `I` play no role; nothing is claimed about regularity across `R = R_h`
of the full metric/potential, nor about the nonlinear (finite-ε) problem.
